text:
emily: Heads up — my Next.js SSR starter (LangChain/Redwood SDK) intermittently returns a 307 during SSR hydration and the SDK client keeps retrying, spiking logs. Happens only when KV cache is enabled in the sample. repo: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-ssr-kv-starter
raj: hmm 307? that's odd. paste the API route + the SSR fetch code. Also which runtime (edge/node) for the API?
emily: API route (simplified):
```js
// pages/api/run.js
import { getServerClient } from '../../lib/redwood'
export default async function handler(req,res){
  const client = getServerClient()
  const out = await client.chat.create({ model: 'l2-small', input: req.body.prompt, useCache: true })
  res.json(out)
}
```
And SSR page calls it server-side during getServerSideProps, then the client hydrates. Logs show: `307 Temporary Redirect` then `redwood-sdk-js retrying request (attempt 2)` and sometimes the response is empty and hydration fails.
sophie: two things to check: 1) 307s usually come from CDN/presigned redirects when auth headers are stripped or the host adds a redirect for large payloads. 2) KV prefix/cache config can cause the SDK to use a different route (cache proxy) which may not accept certain headers on SSR fetch. Can you paste the SDK wrapper (getServerClient) and any fetch options in SSR?
emily: getServerClient is tiny:
```js
// lib/redwood.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
export function getServerClient(){
  return new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, cache: { backend: 'kv', prefix: 'demo' } })
}
```
SSR call is default Next.js getServerSideProps with `fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/run', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }) })` — no special headers.
raj: there it is. On Vercel/Edge/Preview, the internal host may rewrite POSTs to a CDN URL that responds with 307 to redirect to a signed upload endpoint if the body is large or content-type missing. Also if your SDK cache layer sets a special header like `x-redwood-cache: kv` that CDN doesn't like, the CDN may respond with a redirect. The SDK's retry policy then retries the original request which will again hit the redirect loop.
sophie: quick repro: add logging in the API to print incoming headers and body size. Also try setting `Content-Type: application/json` explicitly in your SSR fetch. Many platform proxies rely on that. Example fix: 
```js
// in getServerSideProps
await fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/run', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ prompt })
})
```
And in getServerClient, disable cache prefixing for the demo or use `cache: { backend: 'kv', prefix: null }` to avoid special routing headers.
emily: added Content-Type header and switched cache: { backend: 'kv', prefix: null } locally. Re-deployed to preview and 307s disappeared. Hydration is ok now.
raj: can we make the starter safer by default: server fetches should include Content-Type, and the sample's default cache config should not set a prefix that triggers special proxy behavior. Also add a note about possible platform redirects in README and a small CI smoke test that runs the SSR route and asserts 200 and non-empty HTML.
sophie: i'll open a tiny PR template change to the starter generator to add explicit fetch options in examples and a one-line test.
emily: PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-ssr-kv-starter/pull/21 — includes fix, test, and a dev note about CDN 307s.
devex-bot: Created issue #502 in next-ssr-kv-starter: "SSR hydration 307 from CDN when KV cache prefixing + missing Content-Type; add safer defaults and CI test."
emily: thanks! closing this thread. will also add a short eval harness that runs the SSR path in CI to catch regressions.
